  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d544af41",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Notes for the write-up\n",
    "\n",
    "* **What the numbers mean.** Every metric is computed on **held-out** entities only, averaged over\n",
    "  all link-down scenarios x seeds (mean +/- std). The *topological* rows measure whether the model\n",
    "  faithfully **completes** the injected knowledge over the unknown region; the *demand* rows measure\n",
    "  whether that reasoning also predicts **real traffic impact** (an independent semantic).\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Why AUROC and AUPRC, and why no accuracy.** The held-out sets are strongly imbalanced\n",
    "  (positive rate ~0.21 for links, ~0.14 for nodes under the topological ground truth). A degenerate\n",
    "  \"nothing is affected\" predictor therefore attains 0.79-0.86 accuracy, so accuracy would report the\n",
    "  class prior rather than the inference quality; the same imbalance makes precision/recall/F1 at a\n",
    "  fixed 0.5 cutoff a statement about the LTN sigmoid's calibration rather than its reasoning.\n",
    "  **AUROC** is threshold-free and balance-invariant (chance = 0.5) and admits a direct reading:\n",
    "  given one affected and one unaffected held-out entity, it is the probability the model scores the\n",
    "  affected one higher. **AUPRC** is reported against its correct chance level, the positive rate,\n",
    "  with `AUPRC_lift = AUPRC / PosRate` quantifying the gain over chance; it is the stricter statistic\n",
    "  when negatives dominate, since ranking abundant easy negatives low earns no credit.\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Random-score control.** Every trained model is paired with a random-score baseline evaluated on\n",
    "  the *identical* held-out split, class balance and metric code. Its AUROC concentrates at 0.5 and\n",
    "  its AUPRC at the positive rate, which establishes that the reported margin is attributable to the\n",
    "  learned grounding and not to the evaluation protocol.\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Non-circularity.** Grounding facts use only the *known* entities' topological labels, and the\n",
    "  demand ground truth is never injected into the loss. The sweep asserts that no held-out entity\n",
    "  appears in the known set and that the failed edge is never scored.\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Reproducing Fig. 13 quantitatively.** The Berlin-Hamburg scenario is `L1`; its held-out metrics\n",
    "  are the quantitative analogue of the two-panel figure.\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Runtime.** `len(scenarios) x len(seeds)` training runs. Set `CONFIG['quick_test']=True` for a\n",
    "  smoke run first. GPU recommended for the full 26 x 5 sweep."
   ]
  }
 ],
